This code has all the tasks in the same
main function unlike most of the other homeworks
so it is simply run as 
make 
./main 

and the plots are plotted as
gnuplot plot.gp 
gnuplot uncertaintiesplot.gp 

The code tests the QR decomposition, uses QR to solve 
least-squares problems, fits radioactive decay data, 
computes parameter uncertainties, and makes plots.

Task A1 tests the QR decomposition by checking that R 
is upper triangular, Q^T Q is the identity, and Q R 
reproduces the original matrix.

Task A2 tests the least-squares routine on artificial 
data generated from y = 2 + 3x + x^2.

Task A3 fits radioactive decay data. Since the decay 
model is y = a exp(-lambda t), the code takes logarithms 
and fits ln(y) = ln(a) - lambda t.
The uncertainty in ln(y) is δln(y) = δy/y because the 
derivative of ln(y) is 1/y.

Task A4 writes decay_data.txt and decay_fit.txt, which are 
used by plot.gp to make plot.svg.

Task B computes the covariance matrix of the fit 
parameters and uses it to estimate uncertainties on the 
fitted parameters and on the half-life.

Task C writes decay_band.txt, which is used by 
uncertaintiesplot.gp to plot the best fit together with 
curves made from shifted fit parameters.

AI was used for coding.

The results of running ./main are displayed in results.txt